  "functions": [
    "FUNC.EUROCONVERT"
  ],
  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "EUROCONVERT requires the Euro Currency Tools add-in, coerces TRUE to -1 and VBA literals, and rounds EUR intermediates to 19 places",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, bare =EUROCONVERT(...) returns #NAME? unless EUROTOOL.XLAM is loaded and linked via xlLibrary ([1]!EUROCONVERT). With the add-in loaded, it accepts 18 fixed-rate codes (EUR plus 17 legacy members including GRD, SIT, MTL, CYP, SKK, EEK, rejecting LVL/LTL/HRK/BGN/XEU with #VALUE!), rejects any array, multi-cell range, or worksheet error with #VALUE!, coerces TRUE to -1 and VBA-formatted text (&H, &O, (5), 1-) in number, rounds non-EUR amounts divided by source_rate directly to 19 places (and triangulation_precision >= 3 when supplied, with halves to even), and rounds final outputs to the target currency's places unless full_precision is non-zero. Matches 16,176/16,176 full-bank EUROCONVERT rows.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across 16,176 full-bank EUROCONVERT rows in Excel 16.0.20527 (CalcFunc-Evidence EUROCONVERT.json, eurotool-answers-euroconvert-generated.json, and addin-answers-euroconvert-eurotool.json) and 2,726 workbook rows in crates/calc-host/tests/fixtures/euroconvert/measured.xlsx.",
